In the vein of L's recent "monsters using rings" patch, how about a
patch to allow monsters to use magic whistles?

Now obviously monsters don't have pets, but you could have either
a) any hostile monster using a magic whistle will summon all other
hostile monsters on the level straight over. (ouch)
b) Certain 'heirarchies' are worked out: For example Gnome kings using
whistles will summon all G on the level. Gnome lords can only summon
regular gnomes (not gnome kings, who "outrank" them). Similarly angry
watch captains could summon watchmen (but not vice versa),
sargeants/lieutenants could summon soldiers, elvenkings could summon
elves and so on. Hostile @ can summon hostile dogs, cats and horses. An
orc would summon all other orcs, goblins etc.

Obviously unintelligent/ headless/ non-breathing monsters would not be
able to use the whistle.

This will have the side effect that you can ID magic whistles by
watching NPCs use them. however seeing as how trivial magic whistles
are to ID anyway, I can't see this as an issue.

How do you think cursed magic whistles should work? You could make them
cause a round or two of conflict immediately after use, but that might
be open to abuse (Deliberately leave a cursed whistle where a NPC will
find it inorder to induce conflict). However if the NPCs only whistle
sparingly then the huge influx of monsters would probably be enough to
negate any advantage gained by a round or two of conflict. The conflict
would also apply to tames and peacefuls which further mitigates the
possibility of abuse.

So what do you think then? It would be a fairly small new interaction,
but it stashes another trick up the NPCs' collective sleeve, and it
would make the mines (where tools are generated and left lying around
at random on every level) much more interesting.



